(Technical Whitepaper: Model Fine-Tuning vs RAG Architecture) '
(Author: Enterprise Document Intelligence Group) '
() '
(Executive Overview:) '
(Fine-tuning adjusts internal neural network weights, whereas RAG provides an external,) '
(dynamic non-parametric memory store without model retraining.) '
(For rapidly evolving enterprise documents, RAG is 20x more cost-effective than continuous fine-tuning.) '
() '
(Section 1: Data Freshness & Cost Analysis) '
(Fine-tuning costs approximately $450 to $1,800 per training run on specialized clusters.) '
(In contrast, vector ingestion with DocuMind costs less than $0.002 per document.) '
ET
endstream
